Instantaneous Flow Tracker (IFTA) - License and Usage Notice
==============================================================

Copyright (c) Alexandre Matov. All rights reserved except as granted below.

1. Scope
--------
This repository contains software written or co-written by Alexandre Matov
for the Instantaneous Flow Tracking Algorithm (IFTA), together with several
third-party components used for testing and comparison during development
(see "Third-party components" below). Note also that the core proprietary
optimization/tracking routines have been intentionally omitted from the
publicly available source in this repository -- see the "Repository
contents" section of README.md for details.

2. Permitted use
-----------------
Permission is granted to use, copy, and modify the Alexandre Matov-authored
code in this repository free of charge for research and educational
purposes, provided that:

  a) Any resulting publication, presentation, or derivative work cites the
     relevant paper(s) listed in README.md;
  b) This notice is retained in copies or substantial portions of the code.

Commercial use, redistribution, or incorporation into a commercial product
or service requires prior written permission from Alexandre Matov
(alexandre.matov@gmail.com).

3. No warranty
---------------
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose, and noninfringement. In no event shall
the author be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising
from the use of this software.

4. Third-party components
--------------------------
Several subdirectories bundle or adapt code by other authors, retained here
for reference and comparison and NOT relicensed by the terms above. Each
retains the license/attribution terms of its original author:

  - MaxFlow/            Max-flow implementation by Vladimir Kolmogorov and
                         Yuri Boykov. Historically distributed by the
                         original authors for research/non-commercial use
                         only, with a requirement to cite their papers.
                         Contact the original authors regarding any other
                         use.
  - GoldbergMaxFlow/     Max-flow implementation by Andrew Goldberg,
                         written by Ed Rothberg, distributed via DIMACS.
                         See GoldbergMaxFlow/readme for the original terms.
  - mincost/             Max-flow min-cost implementation based on
  - mincostCPP/          Robert Sedgewick's published algorithm
  - mincostDLL/           ("Algorithms in C++"), adapted by Pascal
                         Vallotton and Alexandre Matov.
  - COSTexe/             Compiled/adapted version of the above.
  - emClustering_Modified_Circular/
                         MATLAB implementation of the mixture-fitting
                         algorithm of M. Figueiredo and A.K. Jain (IEEE
                         2002), circular-clustering modification by
                         Alexandre Matov and Shayan Modiri.

If you are the rights holder of any third-party component listed above and
would like different terms applied, please contact Alexandre Matov.
